The MIT licence in LICENSE covers what is actually ours in this repository:
the setup script, the tools, the analysis summaries and the documentation.
It does NOT cover Hover! itself.

Microsoft Hover! is (c) 1995 Microsoft Corporation, and is not ours to
license. Its executables, data, mazes, textures, sounds and music are not in
this repository and are excluded by .gitignore.

Two consequences worth being explicit about:

  * You need your own copy of the game to use any of this. Setup.cmd copies
    your copy into game/hover; the pipeline reads it from there.

  * Lifted code is a derivative work of the binary it came from.
    Anything this pipeline emits into work/ or src/recomp/gen/ carries whatever
    licence the original carries, not this one. The MIT grant stops at
    our own work.
